\viewkind4\uc1\pard\sa160\sl252\slmult1\i\f0\fs22 Interim Public Works Director Ted Semaan introduced Senior Civil Engineer Eduardo Pech who provided the PowerPoint presentation.\line\line Senior Civil Engineer Pech, Interim Public Works Director Semaan, City Manager Talyn Mirzakhanian, Finance Director Libby Bretthauer, and Traffic Engineer Erik Zandvliet responded to City Council questions.\line\line\cf1 Mayor Lesser opened the floor to public comments. The following individual(s) spoke:\line\line Bob Graham\line Jim Upchurch\line Jerry Johnson\line Thornton Stone\line Barbara Johnson\line Christine Chapman\line Christy Miller\line Ashley Anderson\line\line Seeing no further requests to speak, Mayor Lesser closed the floor to public comments.\line\line Acting City Engineer Gilbert Gamboa, CWE Special Projects Manager Katie Harrel, City Attorney Quinn Barrow, Interim Public Works Director Semaan, Traffic Engineer Zandvliet and Geosyntec Consultants Senior Principal Water Resources Engineer Chris Wessell responded to City Council questions.\cf0\b\i0\line\line A motion was made by Mayor Pro Tem Franklin, regarding the 28th Street Stormwater Infiltration CIP Project, to ensure that the significant concerns are thoroughly addressed and that the project proceeds with the highest level of fiscal responsibility, operational confidence, and timeliness; and to place the project on hold until the financing is fully finalized, a comprehensive parking and traffic study is completed, and additional outreach is conducted with the residents in the affected area.\line\line\b0\i City Attorney Barrow clarified that the City Council could not entertain the motion, as the item was for Receive and File only; and further clarified that the $64,000 fine would not apply to the City of Manhattan Beach, noting instead a standard fine of approximately $10,000 per day; and responded to City Council questions.\line\line\b The City Council Received and Filed the update on the 28\super th\nosupersub  Street Stormwater Infiltration Project (CIP Project No. SW21402).\i0\line\line\pard\b0\i At 8:53 PM, the City Council recessed and reconvened at 9:08 PM with all City Councilmembers present.\cf1\i0\f1\par
